# Restart server yourself

When a change requires a fresh Autologger **server (:8787)** and/or **Vite (:5173)** process (new routes, env, lock/module state, branch switch that changes served code, hot-reload wiped in-memory state, etc.):

- **Do it yourself** — kill the listener(s) if needed, start `npx tsx --env-file-if-exists=.env src/main.ts` from `server/` and/or `npm run dev -w web`, confirm listening.
- **Do not ask** the user to restart, reload “and restart the server,” or leave restart as a manual follow-up.
- A brief note that you restarted is fine; asking them to do it is not.

Vite HMR alone is enough only when the change is purely client-side and already picked up; server-side or branch-checkout work still gets an explicit server restart.
